<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
		<Title>Acumatica REST API for Publishing Customization Packages</Title>
		<Version>6.0.2-preview</Version>
		<Company>Acumatica</Company>
		<Description>An extension for Acumatica REST API client for C# allowing interaction with Customization packages via API</Description>
		<Copyright>Acumatica</Copyright>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Acumatica/AcumaticaRESTAPIClientForCSharp</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Acumatica/AcumaticaRESTAPIClientForCSharp</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageTags>Acumatica;REST;client;</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
		<Authors>Dmitrii-Naumov</Authors>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
6.0.2-preview

The package covers the whole Customization API: Import, GetProject, DeleteProject, PublishBegin, PublishEnd, GetPublished and UnpublishAll, each with an async version, plus WaitPublishingCompletion to wait until publishing is finished. Publishing supports the current tenant, all tenants or a list of tenants (TenantMode and tenantLoginNames). Failed calls throw ApiException with the server's explanation, and a failed publishing throws CustomizationPublishException with the log.

BREAKING CHANGES compared to 6.0.1-preview:
- The extension class is now CustomizationApiExtensions (it had the same name as its namespace).
- CustomizationPublishEnd and CustomizationPublishEndAsync are renamed to PublishEnd and PublishEndAsync.
- CustomizationPublishEnd.isFailed is renamed to IsFailed.
- Import and PublishBegin now return CustomizationResult, which holds the log of the operation (Log, HasErrors). They used to return a single log record, which did not match the server response and came back empty.
- PublishBegin and PublishBeginAsync take IEnumerable of project names instead of List.

FIXES:
- PublishEnd sends a request body. Without it, current servers answered 415 Unsupported Media Type, which also broke WaitPublishingCompletion.
- WaitPublishingCompletion reports a failed publishing even if the server also marks it as completed, and has a timeout. WaitPublishingCompletionAsync supports cancellation.
- Failed calls now throw ApiException that contains the status code and the response body.
- Some failures, such as a project that is not found, are answered by the server with a successful status and an error record in the log. Check CustomizationResult.HasErrors.
- The models follow the 6.0 serialization conventions (no DataContract attributes).
- Built against Acumatica.RESTClient 6.0.2-preview.
		</PackageReleaseNotes>

		<LangVersion>8.0</LangVersion>
		<nullable>Enable</nullable>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="9.0.0">
			<PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
		</PackageReference>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\Acumatica.RESTClient\Acumatica.RESTClient.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
